WEBVTT

00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:02.083
that feels simultaneously
necessary and impossible.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.768
The way trying to fix
racism usually feels.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:09.184
Necessary and impossible.

00:02:09.208 --> 00:02:12.018
So, police chiefs like talking to me
because I'm an expert,

00:02:12.042 --> 00:02:15.018
but I doubt they'd be lining up
to lie down on Dr. Phil's couch

00:02:15.042 --> 00:02:17.309
if I told them all their
problems were hopeless.

00:02:17.333 --> 00:02:19.059
All of my research,

00:02:19.083 --> 00:02:21.476
and the decade of work
I've done with my center --

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.143
the Center for Policing Equity --

00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:25.184
actually leads me to a hopeful conclusion

00:02:25.208 --> 00:02:27.393
amidst all the heartbreak
of race in America,

00:02:27.417 --> 00:02:29.018
which is this:

00:02:29.042 --> 00:02:33.059
trying to solve racism feels impossible